ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: yellow
PROMPT_VERSION: v001
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "wazero v1.12.0", url: "https://github.com/tetratelabs/wazero/blob/v1.12.0/config.go#L651-L660 ; https://github.com/tetratelabs/wazero/blob/v1.12.0/internal/platform/crypto.go ; https://github.com/tetratelabs/wazero/blob/v1.12.0/internal/platform/time.go", overlap: "Ships the core mechanism: default deterministic RandSource, fixed seed 42, fake wall/nano clocks, instant nanosleep; WASI random_get reads this source."},
  {system: "Wasmtime", url: "https://docs.rs/wasmtime-wasi/latest/wasmtime_wasi/struct.WasiCtxBuilder.html#method.secure_random ; https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/main/crates/wasi/src/random.rs", overlap: "Contrasting implementation: default RNG is randomly seeded per context and documented as suitable for WASI security invariants; p1 random_get delegates to get-random-bytes."},
  {system: "Wasmer", url: "https://github.com/wasmerio/wasmer/blob/main/lib/wasix/src/syscalls/wasi/random_get.rs", overlap: "Contrasting implementation: random_get fills bytes via getrandom::fill."},
  {system: "wazero upstream issue #620", url: "https://github.com/wazero/wazero/issues/620", overlap: "Upstream already discussed whether default random_get should be an adequately seeded CSPRNG versus deterministic sandbox-preserving default."},
  {system: "CrowdSec PR #4495", url: "https://github.com/crowdsecurity/crowdsec/pull/4495", overlap: "Practitioner fix adds WithRandSource(crypto/rand.Reader), WithSysWalltime, and WithSysNanotime because wazero defaults made obfuscation byte-identical."},
  {system: "wetware/pkg issue #106", url: "https://github.com/wetware/pkg/issues/106", overlap: "Practitioner independently recognized WithRandSource needs crypto-grade entropy for guests."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: The ABI-level differential holds for the packet’s demonstrated workload and is source-supported: preview1 random_get requires high-quality random data and blocking on insufficient high-quality data (https://github.com/WebAssembly/WASI/blob/snapshot-01/phases/snapshot/docs.md#random_get), while wasi:random 0.2 explicitly requires CSPRNG unpredictability and says deterministic environments must omit the secure API (https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-random/blob/main/wit/random.wit). The realistic-scale gap is prevalence/blast-radius: the packet has real non-zero examples but no authenticated broad code scan, no production incidence rate, and no measured distribution over plugin hosts. vLLM/SGLang/LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM searches produced no material WASI-random/clock overlap, so they do not supply a shipping duplicate or a required baseline for this claim.
RATIONALE: Yellow, not green, because the systems fact pattern is strong but the contribution is a synthesis over already-shipping behavior and already-seen practitioner fixes. Wazero ships the problematic default; Wasmtime and Wasmer show it is a cross-runtime anomaly; WASI specs support the CSPRNG-contract interpretation. However, wazero issue #620, wetware issue #106, and CrowdSec PR #4495 show the mechanism and mitigation were already independently identified in OSS. The remaining contribution is the framed systems insight: ABI-boundary silent demotion plus cross-language/cross-runtime differential plus clock coupling. That is more than glue, but insufficient evidence for green without the L2 prevalence/blast-radius scan and artifact details beyond the summarized 30/30 and 10/10 reproducibility claims.
